  "unit_id": null,
  "baud": null,
  "parity": null,
  "data_bits": null,
  "stop_bits": null,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "1-based",
  "note": "The register tables drop the 4xxxx prefix (register 1 = 40001) and the document says the module is zero-based: 40002 is sent as 0001. Wire address = printed number - 1."
 },
 "default_word_order": "ABCD",
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "MicroTech Unit Controller Protocol Information - Chiller Model WME, C and D-Vintage, and WME-C QUAD (BACnet / Modbus)",
  "doc_number": "ED 19111-4",
  "revision_date": "2026-03",
  "url": "https://tahoeweb.daikinapplied.com/api/general/DownloadDocumentByName/media/19111-4.pdf",
  "pages": "Modbus addressing and data type pp. 8-9; register mapping and word-order example p. 18; Tables 11-14 pp. 19-25; alarm tables pp. 26-35"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Word order: the document's example puts compressor run hours 99900 (0x0001863C) at 74 = 0x0001 and 75 = 0x863C, so two-register values are high word first (ABCD).",
  "'x 10' in a range means the register holds the value times ten, so those registers use scale 0.1. Temperatures and pressures are printed with both English (°F, psi) and metric (°C, kPa) ranges; the English units are shown here. The document's units selector is described for BACnet only, so check which unit system the Modbus values use on site.",
  "Signedness is not stated: a register is typed INT16 when its published range goes below zero, otherwise UINT16.",
  "Compressor Off/Auto (1841, 1827, 1801, 1788) is typed RW in the data-type column but R in the access column; it is listed read-only. The WME-C needs chiller application code 1.2.4 or newer for these registers.",
  "Left out: the alarm module ID/type/payload registers (2001-2009), which are explained only in the BACnet alarm sections; communication defaults, because the Table 1 Modbus column is misaligned in the source (see Daikin IM 1283 for network setup).",
  "For Ice and Heat modes only Cool applies on WME-C and WME-D."
 ],
